From: SAGA <saga@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] block/adios: deadline bonus for latency-critical IO priority (top-app)

Incremental on top of the "adios" addon (adios-android14-6.1-v3.2.0.patch).
Requires that addon to have already run in the same ADDONS= list --
context is the post-adios state of block/adios.c. NOT verified against
"adios-tunable" (0002-adios-tunable-lm-and-persist-android.patch) which
also touches add_to_dl_tree() and struct adios_data -- if you use both
adios and adios-tunable, re-check this patch applies before adios-
tunable clashes with the same anchor lines; your current ADDONS list
(per your build.yml) does not include adios-tunable, so this was built
and verified against plain "adios" only.

This is the ADIOS-side counterpart to the BORE top-app work
(bore-topapp, 0001/0002 above): the same "the scheduler doesn't know
which task matters, only its behavior" gap exists here. add_to_dl_tree()
computes each request's deadline purely from its start time, op type,
and the adaptive latency model -- it has no notion of which process
issued it.

Unlike the CPU scheduler, ADIOS's struct request does not carry a
cgroup reference (block cgroups/blkcg are a separate controller
attachment from the task's cpu/uclamp cgroup, and by the time a bio
reaches the elevator the submitting task_struct is not reliably
available -- writeback, io threads, and merged bios all break that
link). So this patch does NOT reuse task_group()->latency_sensitive
the way the BORE patches do -- that signal isn't available at this
layer. Instead it reads req_get_ioprio(rq), the IO priority already
carried on struct request (rq->ioprio, set from the submitting bio at
allocation time -- see include/linux/blk-mq.h). This is the same
signal BFQ and mq-deadline already use for exactly this purpose.

Whether this actually helps in your case depends on whether your
Android build sets IO priority for the top-app cgroup. Some AOSP-
derived task_profiles.json configs do this via an IoSchedClass/
SetIoPriority-style action so top-app runs at IOPRIO_CLASS_RT or a low
IOPRIO_CLASS_BE level; many stock configs leave it at default
(IOPRIO_CLASS_NONE, no boost). If your device's task_profiles.json
doesn't set it, this patch compiles and runs fine but adios_req_is_topapp()
never returns true, so it's a safe no-op -- worth checking with
`cat /proc/<top-app pid>/io` -> ioprio, or grepping your vendor
task_profiles.json for "IoSched" / "IoPriority", before expecting an
effect.

Change: adios_req_is_topapp() classifies a request as latency-critical
if its ioprio class is IOPRIO_CLASS_RT, or IOPRIO_CLASS_BE at level 0-1
(the top of that class's 8 levels). add_to_dl_tree() then subtracts a
bounded, sysfs-tunable nanosecond bonus (topapp_deadline_bonus,
default 4ms, exposed the same way as ADIOS's other tunables via
SYSFS_ULL_DECL) from the computed deadline before it's inserted into
the RB-tree -- moving it earlier in dispatch order. Applies to both
sync (Tier 2) and async (Tier 3) requests, since both branches set
rd->deadline before the quantization step this hooks into. Bounded by
min_t so it can never push a deadline negative/wrap.

Verified: applied cleanly (zero rejects, zero fuzz) on top of a freshly
regenerated block/adios.c from the real adios-android14-6.1-v3.2.0.patch.

Signed-off-by: SAGA <saga@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/block/adios.c b/block/adios.c
+++ b/block/adios.c
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <linux/string.h>
 #include <linux/list_sort.h>
 #include <linux/rcupdate.h>
+#include <linux/ioprio.h>
 
 #include "elevator.h"
 #include "blk.h"
@@ -114,6 +115,7 @@
 };
 
 // Latency targets for each operation type
+static u64 default_topapp_deadline_bonus = 4 * NSEC_PER_MSEC;
 static u64 default_latency_target[ADIOS_OPTYPES] = {
 	[ADIOS_READ]    =     2ULL * NSEC_PER_MSEC,
 	[ADIOS_WRITE]   =  2000ULL * NSEC_PER_MSEC,
@@ -246,6 +248,7 @@
 	u64 global_latency_window;
 	u64 compliance_flags;
 	u64 latency_target[ADIOS_OPTYPES];
+	u64 topapp_deadline_bonus;
 	u32 batch_limit[ADIOS_OPTYPES];
 	u32 batch_actual_max_size[ADIOS_OPTYPES];
 	u32 batch_actual_max_total;
@@ -712,6 +715,25 @@
 static inline u32 eval_adios_state(struct adios_data *ad, u32 shift)
 { return eval_this_adios_state(get_adios_state(ad), shift); }
 
+/*
+ * True when the request's IO priority marks it as belonging to a
+ * latency-critical submitter -- RT class outright, or the top tiers
+ * of the BE class (Android's task_profiles.json commonly assigns one
+ * of these to the top-app cgroup via ioprio_set()/SetIoPriority when
+ * configured to do so; harmless no-op otherwise, since default class
+ * for unconfigured processes is IOPRIO_CLASS_NONE/BE-4).
+ */
+static inline bool adios_req_is_topapp(struct request *rq) {
+	unsigned short ioprio = req_get_ioprio(rq);
+	unsigned short class = IOPRIO_PRIO_CLASS(ioprio);
+
+	if (class == IOPRIO_CLASS_RT)
+		return true;
+	if (class == IOPRIO_CLASS_BE && IOPRIO_PRIO_DATA(ioprio) <= 1)
+		return true;
+	return false;
+}
+
 // Add a request to the deadline-sorted red-black tree
 static void add_to_dl_tree(
 		struct adios_data *ad, bool dl_idx, struct request *rq) {
@@ -737,6 +759,9 @@
 			rd->deadline += rd->pred_lat;
 	}
 
+	if (ad->topapp_deadline_bonus && adios_req_is_topapp(rq))
+		rd->deadline -= min_t(u64, rd->deadline, ad->topapp_deadline_bonus);
+
 	// Now quantize the deadline (-> dlg->deadline == RB-Tree key)
 	deadline = rd->deadline & ~((1ULL << ADIOS_QUANTUM_SHIFT) - 1);
 
@@ -1600,6 +1625,7 @@
 		ad->latency_target[optype] = default_latency_target[optype];
 		ad->batch_limit[optype] = default_batch_limit[optype];
 	}
+	ad->topapp_deadline_bonus = default_topapp_deadline_bonus;
 
 	eq->elevator_data = ad;
 
@@ -1833,6 +1859,7 @@
 
 SYSFS_ULL_DECL(global_latency_window, 0, ULLONG_MAX)
 SYSFS_ULL_DECL(compliance_flags, 0, ULLONG_MAX)
+SYSFS_ULL_DECL(topapp_deadline_bonus, 0, NSEC_PER_SEC)
 
 #define SYSFS_INT_DECL(field, min_val, max_val) \
 static ssize_t adios_##field##_show( \
@@ -2023,6 +2050,7 @@
 	AD_ATTR_RW(shrink_resist),
 
 	AD_ATTR_RW(read_priority),
+	AD_ATTR_RW(topapp_deadline_bonus),
 
 	AD_ATTR_WO(reset_bq_stats),
 	AD_ATTR_WO(reset_lat_model),
